{
  "_readme": "Shared projection cases (P1-7, D18). Read by tests/test_projection.py on the server and by web/src/__tests__/projection.test.ts in the browser suite. Both implementations must agree on every case, so a rule that changes on one side and not the other fails a test instead of confusing a writer's table of contents. Expected values are hand-written: they are the specification, not a recording of what the code happens to do. The `blocks` key is the block index (P2-5): the same cases seen in both coordinate systems, hand-derived from ProseMirror's position arithmetic. The client mirror has no index and reads named keys, so it ignores it.",
